# Code of Conduct — ProjectName

## Our Commitment

We are committed to providing a welcoming, respectful, and inclusive environment for everyone contributing to or interacting with ProjectName.

We welcome contributions regardless of experience, background, nationality, gender, identity, beliefs, or personal circumstances.

## Expected Behavior

All participants are expected to:

- Be respectful, considerate, and constructive.
- Respect different perspectives and experiences.
- Communicate professionally and respectfully.
- Accept constructive criticism.
- Focus on what is best for the project and its community.
- Help maintain a welcoming environment for newcomers.

## Unacceptable Behavior

The following behaviors are not acceptable:

- Harassment, discrimination, or intimidation.
- Insults, personal attacks, or deliberately hostile behavior.
- Hate speech or discriminatory language.
- Publishing private information without consent.
- Trolling, spam, or deliberately disruptive behavior.
- Any other conduct that creates an unsafe or hostile environment.

## Enforcement

Project maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing this Code of Conduct.

Depending on the severity of the violation, maintainers may:

- Issue a warning.
- Remove inappropriate content.
- Temporarily restrict participation.
- Permanently ban individuals from participating in the project.

## Reporting

If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, please contact the project maintainers privately through an appropriate GitHub channel.

All reports will be handled as respectfully and confidentially as reasonably possible.

## Scope

This Code of Conduct applies to all ProjectName project spaces, including GitHub repositories, discussions, pull requests, issues, and other community-related interactions.

## Acknowledgment

By participating in ProjectName, you agree to follow this Code of Conduct.

We believe open-source projects should be built through respect, collaboration, and shared responsibility.